      "id": 491763,
      "username": "Ayesha_F",
      "name": null,
      "created_at": "2026-01-19T10:38:20.261Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Options for overriding a Python function:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>If it is a whitelisted method, use the <strong>override_whitelisted_methods</strong> hook.</li>\n<li>If it is a standard doctype classes , use <strong>override_doctype_class</strong> hook.</li>\n<li>For document methods and events, use <strong>doc_events</strong> hook.</li>\n<li>If it falls outside these options, you can use <strong>monkey patching</strong>. <a href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/t/frappe-monkey-patching-guide-overriding-change-core-code-without-touching-it/148237\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Frappe Monkey Patching Guide: Overriding/Change Core Code Without Touching it</a></li>\n</ol>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/9de053/{size}.png",
